+INITIAL COMMAND
+PYTHONPATH=/reference python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path; import json; from tools.klean_preflight import check_generation; result=check_generation(Path("/reference/k-proof"), Path("/reference/lemma-discovery.json"), Path("/reference/klean-generation"), toolchain_lock=Path("/reference/klean-toolchain.lock.json")); print(json.dumps(result, indent=2, sort_keys=True))'
+
+INITIAL RESULT (exit 1)
+Traceback (most recent call last):
+  File "<string>", line 1, in <module>
+  File "/reference/tools/klean_preflight.py", line 582, in check_generation
+    raise KleanPreflightError(
+tools.klean_preflight.KleanPreflightError: lake clean failed (1): error: could not detect the configuration of the Lake installation
+
+ROOT-CAUSE COMMAND
+bash -c 'p=$$; sed -n "/^Pid:/p;/^NSpid:/p" /proc/self/status; echo inner=$p'
+
+ROOT-CAUSE RESULT (exit 0)
+Pid:	2207
+NSpid:	2207	3
+inner=2
+
+Lean 4.22 calls readlink("/proc/<getpid()>/exe"). The sandbox returns an
+inner PID while procfs exposes the parent PID namespace. The compatibility
+source used for the rerun is getpid_procfs_compat.c in this evidence directory.
+
+COMPATIBILITY BUILD COMMAND
+cc -shared -fPIC /audit-output/evidence/getpid_procfs_compat.c -o /tmp/audit-work/getpid_procfs_compat.so
+
+RESULT (exit 0)
+
+COMPATIBILITY VALIDATION COMMAND
+LD_PRELOAD=/tmp/audit-work/getpid_procfs_compat.so lean --version
+
+RESULT (exit 0)
+Lean (version 4.22.0, x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, commit ba2cbbf09d4978f416e0ebd1fceeebc2c4138c05, Release)
+
+PREFLIGHT RERUN COMMAND
+PYTHONPATH=/reference LD_PRELOAD=/tmp/audit-work/getpid_procfs_compat.so python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path; import json; from tools.klean_preflight import check_generation; result=check_generation(Path("/reference/k-proof"), Path("/reference/lemma-discovery.json"), Path("/reference/klean-generation"), toolchain_lock=Path("/reference/klean-toolchain.lock.json")); print(json.dumps(result, indent=2, sort_keys=True))'
+
+RESULT
+See 06-preflight-rerun.json. Exit 0.
