+/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k:154:  rule applyCmp("==", V:Val, noneV) => V ==K noneV
+/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k:155:  rule applyCmp("!=", V:Val, noneV) => notBool (V ==K noneV)
+/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k:203:  rule applyCmp("<", I:Int, F:Float) => floatLt(intToF(I), F)
+/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k:204:  rule applyCmp("<", F:Float, I:Int) => floatLt(F, intToF(I))
+/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k:205:  rule applyCmp(">", I:Int, F:Float) => gtF(intToF(I), F)
+/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k:206:  rule applyCmp(">", F:Float, I:Int) => gtF(F, intToF(I))
+
+Other frozen modules also define applyCmp for Bool, String, List, Set, and
+Dict. The candidate implements only "=="/">" with a Float right operand and
+returns false otherwise.
